1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jiang Qing''' was the pseudonym that was used by Chinese leader Mao Zedong's last wife and major Communist Party of China power figure. She went by the stage name '''Lan Ping''' (Chinese: 蓝苹) during her acting c
2 CONC areer, and was known by various other names during her life. She married Mao in Yan'an in November 1938, and is sometimes referred to as '''Madame Mao''' in Western literature, serving as Communist China's first first lady. Jiang 
2 CONC Qing was most well known for playing a major role in the Cultural Revolution (1966–76) and for forming the radical political alliance known as the "Gang of Four". She was named the "Great Flag-carrier of the Proletarian Culture" (
2 CONC 无产阶级文艺伟大旗手/無產階級文藝偉大旗手).
