1 NAME Chew Yook /Hong/
2 GIVN Chew Yook
2 _MARNM Hong
2 NICK 湯恩明
1 NAME Chew Yook Hong 曾稠毓 138, 126, 73, 69, 16世
1 NAME 曾 /稠毓/ 138, 126, 73, 69, 16世
2 GIVN 曾
2 SURN 稠毓
2 NSFX 138, 126, 73, 69, 16世
2 NICK 湯恩明
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 11 MAY 1870
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dong An
3 STAE Guangdong
3 CTRY China
1 DEAT
2 DATE JUL 1941
2 ADDR
3 CTRY China
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chew Yook was born in China and first traveled to America when he was 16 years old. There are no official records of his arrival, but according to family members, he probably entered the country illegally.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime after his arrival, he purchased the papers for Hong Yin Ming, who was a natural born U.S. citizen, having been born in San Francisco in 1873.  The decendants of Chew Yook have used the surname Hong ever since.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to U.S. District court records, the real Hong Yin Ming went to China with his mother when he was very young, and returned to U.S. in 1888.  At that time, he sued in court to be allowed to landed.  What happened to him af
2 CONC ter the court ruled in his favor, we do not know.
2 CONT
2 CONT We do know that Chew Yook returned to China when he in 1899 to get married, leaving the United States under the name Hong Yin Ming.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hock How was born on June 6, 1900, and Chew Yook left for America shortly thereafter.  Chew Yook returned to China in 1903.  Quong How as born August 27, 1904.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Chew Yook was back in America from 1905-1913, then made his final trip the the U.S. in 1915 with Hock How.  While in America, Chew Yook worked as a cook out in Palo Alto, California, which at the time was consider to be out in the
2 CONC  country.  Quang How joined his father and brother in America in 1923.
2 CONT
2 CONT After living in America for 40 of the past 46 years, Chew Yook returned to China in 1932 at the age of 63.  He died in July 1941 in Dong An (Ong On), Guangdong, the village where he was born. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dong An has since been incorporated into the larger village of Qí Lè, Taishan, Guangdong (廣東省台山縣其樂村, 22°02'26.3"N 112°49'50.4"E).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note on Chew Yook’s Paper Sons:  
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his two biological sons, Chew Yook also had three paper sons.  Nephews Jeong Hing and Chun Mao were two of them.  Ning Bo, grandson of Shou Qiu and the son of one of Chew Yook’s first cousins, was the third.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ning Bo, the eldest paper son, lived in America from 1909 to 1937, when he died in his fifties.  Chun Mao came to America with Quong How in 1923.  Jeong Hing tried to enter the U.S. in 1931, but was denied entry and returned to Ch
2 CONC ina.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note on Generation Numbers (138, 126, 73, 69, 16世)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Chew Yook is a 138th generation descendant of [http://www.geni.com/people/Hu%C3%A1ng-D%C3%AC-%E9%BB%84%E5%B8%9D-J%C4%AB-Xu%C4%81n-Yu%C3%A1n-%E5%A7%AC%E8%BB%92%E8%BD%85-1/6000000001381274001 Huang Di (the Yellow Emperor)], and foll
2 CONC owing the same line of descent:
2 CONT
2 CONT * a 126th generation descendant of [http://www.geni.com/people/Z%C4%93ng-Q%C5%AB-Li%C3%A8-%E9%84%AB%E6%9B%B2%E7%83%88-13-1%E4%B8%96/6000000019932971265 Zēng Qū Liè 鄫曲烈, 13, 1世], who was the first to the name Zēng
2 CONT * a 73th generation descendant of [http://www.geni.com/people/Z%C4%93ng-W%C5%AB-%E6%9B%BE%E5%B7%AB-66-54-1%E4%B8%96/6000000019933189985 Zēng Wū 曾巫, 66, 54, 1世], who was the first to use the simplified version of Zēng
2 CONT * a 69st generation descendant of the Confucian disciple, [http://www.geni.com/people/Z%C4%93ng-Sh%C4%93n-%E6%9B%BE%E5%8F%83-70-58-5-1%E4%B8%96/6000000013859213357 Zēng Shēn 曾參, 70, 58, 5, 1世]
2 CONT * a 16th generation descendant of [http://www.geni.com/people/Z%C4%93ng-Zi-R%C3%B3ng-%E6%9B%BE%E5%AD%90%E6%A6%AE-123-111-58-54-1%E4%B8%96/6000000002982093499 Zēng Zi Róng 曾子榮 123, 111, 58, 54, 1世] who establish the branch of the f
2 CONC amily in Tai Shan County, Guangdong, China
2 CONT * Chew Yook was the first member of his family to live in the United States and adopt the surname Hong
