1 NAME Cheng Tiong /KHOO 邱/
2 GIVN Cheng Tiong
2 SURN KHOO 邱
2 _MARNM KHOO 邱
2 NICK Khoo Tock Xin
2 NICK 邱笃信
2 NICK KHOO Cheng Teong
1 NAME KHOO Cheng Tiong, 邱正忠, 18世
1 NAME 正忠 //
2 GIVN 正忠
2 SURN 邱
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 PLAC Hai Teng
2 ADDR
3 CTRY China
1 DEAT
2 DATE JUN 1896
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/Digitised/Article/singfreepressb19180518-1.2.16.2?ST=1&AT=search&k=KHOO%20Yang%20Tin&P=4&Display=0&filterS=0&QT=khoo,yang,tin&oref=article
2 CONT
2 CONT http://api.sg/forums/topic/oldest-chinese-tomb-in-singapore/
2 CONT
2 CONT The early pioneers of Singapore that also come from 新垵 is Khoo Cheng Tiong (邱正忠 or 邱笃信). He was born in 1820 and come to singapore in 1840. He might be a relative or contempatory of 邱正直, as he and his brothers first two characters
2 CONC  are 邱正.
2 CONT
2 CONT Khoo Cheng Tiong (邱正忠) is a famous Singapore rice merchant and was the president of Thong Chia Medial Institution. His 3rd brother Khoo Cheng Cheok 邱正朝 even has a street Cheng Cheok Street (at Tanjong Pagar previously) named after
2 CONC  him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Khoo Cheng Tiong is also the father of Khoo Siok Guan (邱菽园), the famous scholar poet in Singapore, who started the Tian Nan Press in 1898, was an editor of Sin Chew Jit Poh and died in 1941
2 CONT
2 CONT The other tomb which is of a couple, the wife of of an Eurasian. Their daughter is called “Holland”. The daughter must have married a brother of the Khoo family or very close relative because their descandents share a common name 
2 CONC for the first 2 characters: 邱睛. That is why they can be buried at the same area.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT of Singapore
2 CONT
