2 CONT https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/Digitised/Article/straitstimes19250624-1.2.21?ST=1&AT=advanced&DF=&DT=16%2f06%2f1950&NPT=&L=&CTA=&K=Khoo+Sin+Hoe&KA=Khoo+Sin+Hoe&P=3&Display=0&filterS=0&QT=khoo,sin,hoe&oref=article
2 CONT
2 CONT https://thelongnwindingroad.wordpress.com/?s=hun+yeang+road
2 CONT
2 CONT http://malayan-b-m-d.blogspot.sg/search?q=khoo+Hun+Yeang
2 CONT
2 CONT http://overseaschineseinthebritishempire.blogspot.sg/2013/02/khoo-hun-yeang.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://overseaschineseinthebritishempire.blogspot.my/search/label/Khoo%20Sian%20Tan
2 CONT
2 CONT Khoo Hun Yeang was born in Penang in 1860 to Khoo Thean Teik. His father was a prominent figure in Penang and Perak. Khoo Hun Yeang was educated in Penang and joined his father's business in coconut plantation in Province Wellesle
2 CONC y.  He managed the business successfully for 10 years and returned to Penang to assist her father's interest in the Penang Opium and Spirit Farm in which he remained for another 6 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Khoo Hun Yeang later commenced business on his own account in Penang under the firm chop Chin Lee & Co., trading in tin and general trades. In 1899 he joined the Singapore Opium and Spirit Farm, and was appointed managing director
2 CONC  of the farm from 1902 until 1906. He relinquished his interest in the Singapore farm and went to Kuching to venture in the construction industry. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Khoo Hun Yeang was the Vice-Chairman of the Penang Chinese Town Hall, a Board Member of the Kek Lok Si Temple and the Cheng Hoon Giam Temple (Snake Temple). The main street, Khoo Hun Yeang Road, in which he built in Kuching was na
2 CONC med after him. He died in Medan in 1917 and was buried in Kampung Bahru, Penang, at his family burial ground. He was survived by a principal wife Ong Gek Chai (王玉钗), 8 sons, his two elder sons Khoo Siew Jin (b. 1884) and Khoo Siew
2 CONC  Ghee were prominent merchants in Singapore.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/straitsechomail19260119-1.2.20?qt=gan,%20teong,%20eng&q=GAN%20Teong%20Eng
