1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moh Guan Terrace in Tiong Bahru is named after him.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the fourth son of See Hood Kee and hIs brother was SEE Eng Watt.  They operated a business under the name Eng Wat, Moh Guan and Brothers, Chop Kim Hin at No. 10 Boat Quay.  It was reported in The Straits Times of 20 June 18
2 CONC 54, page 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT The brothers involved were Eng Wat, Moh Guan, Koon Guan and Teh Guan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moh Guan was apparently in the pepper and gambier business.  He was also the Chairman of the Heng Shan Ting temple.
