1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Syed Mohamed Alatas, a wealthy Acehnese merchant of Arab descent
2 CONT
2 CONT Syed Mohamed Alatas was a wealthy merchant from Aceh on the island of Summatra, who traded between Aceh and Penang. He was a key figure in helping the Acehnese resist the Dutch seige of 1870 by smuggling arms to the resistance.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived in this house on Lebuh Armenian, near the junction with Lebuh Acheh, with his first wife, a Malay of royal descent. His second wife was the daughter of the head of the Khoo clan
2 CONT
