1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Ewe Lay descended from an old Peranakan family in Malacca. He moved to Singapore and became comprador for the Hongkong and Shanghai Bank. In 1881, he started, Lat Pau 叻报, the first major Chinese-language daily 
2 CONC newspaper in Singapore; it continued to be published until 1934. This demonstrates that English-oriented Peranakans were still intimately involved in Chinese-language culture
