1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Municipal Commissioner / Penang Free School''' / 2nd son
2 CONT
2 CONT '''KHOO Sian Ewe J.P. of Sunbeam Hall, Light Street'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Khoo Sian Ewe Road, or Jalan Khoo Sian Ewe, is a short road linking Phee Choon Road with Burmah Road (Jalan Burma). It was built in the early 20th Century and was named after the philanthropic land proprietor Khoo Sian Ewe (1886-1
2 CONC 964) who owned the land on both sides of Khoo Sian Ewe Road.
2 CONT
2 CONT Khoo Sian Ewe was the second son of Kapitan China Khoo Cheow Teong from Sumatra. He was a student of the Penang Free School and later served as one of the first vice-presidents and second president (1924-38) of the Old Frees' Asso
2 CONC ciation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography:
